        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://postlakeswi.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Sokaogon Ojibwe tribe were the first known inhabitants to live along the shores of Upper Post Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://postlakeswi.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Chief Sa-Wa-Ba-She-She once established a headquarters for councils and ceremonies at Post Lake for a Chippewa band of 700 members.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/post_lake_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The name of the Sokaogon Chippewa Community derives from a spiritual post located at Post Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/post_lake_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Post Lake hosted a local post office from 1884 until it was discontinued in 1913.",
